Let's see if I understand two items -

1) Damage done by magic missiles.  Gets higher as your level gets
higher.  Like all spells has a higher chance of success when wearing a
robe.  Like a list of spells gets doubled when you carry the Magic
Mirror.  I get why you can end up taking out a level 20 mastadon with a
single shot.

Knights can end up blasting away with far more power than a giant stack
of highly enchanted daggers (which they can't because of spell limits).

2) MR as the monster's magic resistance.  Is this the percentage of
times they are immune to damage from a magic missile hit?  If so then
the list of monsters with 100% resistance is telling: Rodney and the
Riders.  Then I don't get why finger of death works on Rodney.  Above I
used mastadon as an example because it was the highest level of monster
with an MR=0.  Examples of monsters with MR=90 read like a list of the
ones you don't want to meet in a dark corridor.  Both types of mind
flayer, ki-rin, master and arch liches, Asmodeus.  Demogorgon even has
MR=95.

Do I read that right as meaning mind flayers and such get no effect at
all from a migic missile hit 90% of the time and the other 10% of the
time they get the full damage?

If that's how it works I'd want to blast away at a crowd to thin out
vulnerable members and then start using other means to take out the
resistant ones.  But I don't think I have it right because I've zapped
Rodney with a wand of death and it worked.  Unless magic missile and
finger of death use different resistances?


